        history: {
          origins: 'Stop the Bus is a British draw-and-discard game in the commerce family. It shares mechanisms with Commerce (18th century) and Thirty-One (Scat), in which players draw and discard to improve a three-card hand. The version documented here was contributed by Nic Cleveland from Guernsey; the name is also used for a Thirty-One variant (Ride the Bus) and for Bastard Brag, which uses table exchange instead of stock and discard.',
          originCountries: [
